# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# OPEN positive. One callable formal receives held definitions made by two
# methods, each formed in its own way, and two copies of one of them. ga
# reads n; gb reads m. pa and pa2 hold ga with n 100 and n 200; pb holds gb
# with m 30. run calls its formal: 105, 205 and 60. under has n 1 and m 2:
# 6 and 6 for the two copies of ga, 4 for gb. This implementation does not
# tell the node of one definition from the node of another where the call
# is made: the call in run is refused where it stands, as a limit and no
# rule. Entry 7.
fn: f0 () int
    return: 1
end: f0

fn: makeA (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: ga () int
        return: n + 5
    return: ga

fn: makeB (int: m) fn: () int
    fn: gb () int
        return: m * 2
    return: gb

@: pa makeA(100)
@: pa2 makeA(200)
@: pb makeB(30)

fn: run (f0: q) int
    return: q()
end: run

fn: under () int
    int: n 1
    int: m 2
    return: run(pa) * 10000 + run(pa2) * 100 + run(pb)
end: under

int: a run(pa)
int: b run(pa2)
int: c run(pb)
int: d under()
int: ok 7
if: a != 105 || b != 205 || c != 60 || d != 60604
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
